{"id":"MRP-031","claim":"Room 21 °C / 65 %RH ≈ 10.1 g/kg, dew point ≈ 14.2 °C; at a 15 °C wall the surface RH ≈ 95%.","claim_class":"psychrometric","surface":"course:mould-remediation-fundamentals#00e0238a-7eb4-4380-aae3-2c5880730879","status":"JUSTIFIED","confidence":"high","reasoning":"DERIVED: Hyland-Wexler p_ws(21 °C) = 2.488 kPa; p_v = 0.65 x 2.488 = 1.617 kPa; W = 10.09 g/kg; dew point 14.2 °C; p_ws(15 °C) = 1.705 kPa; 1.617 / 1.705 = 94.8%. Areas 1.1 x 0.6 = 0.66 and 1.2 x 0.8 = 0.96, total 1.62 m².","best_available_source":"Hyland-Wexler saturation vapour pressure formulation (ASHRAE Handbook - Fundamentals, Psychrometrics chapter), cited by name","feeds":["course:mould-remediation-fundamentals"],"lesson_id":"00e0238a-7eb4-4380-aae3-2c5880730879","part":"mechanism","evidence_grade":"A2","also_in":["course:mould-remediation-fundamentals#quiz:bf91664e-08b5-4ea0-9ec3-e9eae89128a9","course:mould-remediation-fundamentals#quiz:ce8d62e3-21da-47a9-b987-d627d1b25c22"]}
{"id":"MRP-032","claim":"Where mould is visible, testing is generally not considered necessary; an occupational hygienist can help where contamination is suspected but the source cannot be found.","claim_class":"method","surface":"course:mould-remediation-fundamentals#00e0238a-7eb4-4380-aae3-2c5880730879","status":"VERIFIED","source_url":"https://www.betterhealth.vic.gov.au/health/ConditionsAndTreatments/mould-and-your-health","access_date":"2026-11-02","quote":"you could employ an occupational hygienist or environmental health and safety professional","feeds":["course:mould-remediation-fundamentals"],"lesson_id":"00e0238a-7eb4-4380-aae3-2c5880730879","part":"evidence","evidence_grade":"A2","check_by":"2027-05-02","also_in":["course:mould-remediation-fundamentals#field-tool:area-decision-and-failure-check.md"]}
{"id":"MRP-033","claim":"Moulds release spores when disturbed, such as during cleaning, or in dry conditions when a building is being dried out.","claim_class":"method","surface":"course:mould-remediation-fundamentals#3dae611c-dd3d-49d3-9cb9-b1251ed1aafa","status":"VERIFIED","source_url":"https://nt.gov.au/wellbeing/healthy-living/mould-growth","access_date":"2026-11-02","quote":"This happens when moulds are disturbed, such as during cleaning, or in dry conditions when a house or building is being dried out.","feeds":["course:mould-remediation-fundamentals"],"lesson_id":"3dae611c-dd3d-49d3-9cb9-b1251ed1aafa","part":"evidence","evidence_grade":"A2","check_by":"2027-05-02","also_in":["course:mould-remediation-fundamentals#quiz:bf91664e-08b5-4ea0-9ec3-e9eae89128a9","course:mould-remediation-fundamentals#quiz:ce8d62e3-21da-47a9-b987-d627d1b25c22","course:mould-remediation-fundamentals#field-tool:area-decision-and-failure-check.md"]}
