{"id":"MRP-035","claim":"Abrasive cleaning such as dry brushing is not recommended because it can release spores into the air.","claim_class":"method","surface":"course:mould-remediation-fundamentals#3dae611c-dd3d-49d3-9cb9-b1251ed1aafa","status":"VERIFIED","source_url":"https://www.health.qld.gov.au/public-health/disaster/public-health-advice/mould","access_date":"2026-11-02","quote":"it is not recommended to abrasively clean mould from a surface, such as with a dry brush, as this could release spores into the air","feeds":["course:mould-remediation-fundamentals"],"lesson_id":"3dae611c-dd3d-49d3-9cb9-b1251ed1aafa","part":"evidence","evidence_grade":"A2","check_by":"2027-05-02","also_in":["course:mould-remediation-fundamentals#quiz:ce8d62e3-21da-47a9-b987-d627d1b25c22"]}
{"id":"MRP-036","claim":"Failure arithmetic: Monday 7 pm to Friday 9 am = 86 h; 25 °C / 72 %RH ≈ 14.3 g/kg vs 24 °C / 55 %RH ≈ 10.2 g/kg, a 4.1 g/kg difference.","claim_class":"psychrometric","surface":"course:mould-remediation-fundamentals#3dae611c-dd3d-49d3-9cb9-b1251ed1aafa","status":"JUSTIFIED","confidence":"high","reasoning":"DERIVED: 96 h - 10 h = 86 h; Hyland-Wexler W(25, 72) = 14.33, W(24, 55) = 10.24 g/kg; 14.3 - 10.2 = 4.1. Scenario figures illustrative.","best_available_source":"Hyland-Wexler saturation vapour pressure formulation (ASHRAE Handbook - Fundamentals, Psychrometrics chapter), cited by name","feeds":["course:mould-remediation-fundamentals"],"lesson_id":"3dae611c-dd3d-49d3-9cb9-b1251ed1aafa","part":"mechanism","evidence_grade":"A2","also_in":["course:mould-remediation-fundamentals#quiz:bf91664e-08b5-4ea0-9ec3-e9eae89128a9","course:mould-remediation-fundamentals#quiz:ce8d62e3-21da-47a9-b987-d627d1b25c22"]}
{"id":"MRP-037","claim":"The six failure patterns (cause not fixed, porous material kept, air moved before containment, dust left, rebuilt wet, no record) are the common causes of callbacks.","claim_class":"method","surface":"course:mould-remediation-fundamentals#3dae611c-dd3d-49d3-9cb9-b1251ed1aafa","status":"GAP","reason":"The callback review is an illustrative composite, not a measured study. Each failure is tied to a regulator source or Level 2 lesson, but the claim that these are the most common causes has no data behind it. SME to confirm from CARSI field experience, or soften to \"failures we see\".","recommended_action":"substantiate","feeds":["course:mould-remediation-fundamentals"],"lesson_id":"3dae611c-dd3d-49d3-9cb9-b1251ed1aafa","part":"requirement","also_in":["course:mould-remediation-fundamentals#field-tool:area-decision-and-failure-check.md"]}
